 1. JSON.generate is compact, and Symbols become Strings       {"a":1,"b":[1,2.5,null,true],"c":"sym"}
 2. to_json on a Hash, Array, String, nil, Symbol, Float       {"a":1} [1,"two"] "str" null "sym" 1.5
 3. JSON.pretty_generate({a: 1, b: [1, 2]}):                   
      {
        "a": 1,
        "b": [
          1,
          2
        ]
      }
 4. JSON.parse gives String keys                               {"a" => 1, "b" => [1, 2.5, nil, true]}
 5.   symbolize_names: true gives Symbol keys                  {a: 1}
 6. a Symbol value comes back as a String                      {"a" => "sym"}
 7. non-String keys are stringified: {1 => 2, nil => 3}        {"1":2,"":3}
 8. a scalar document: parse of 3, "s", null                   [3, "s", nil]
 9. duplicate keys: the last one wins                          {"a" => 2}
10. bad input raises; its ancestors                            JSON::ParserError < JSON::JSONError < StandardError
11. NaN is not JSON: generate raises                           JSON::GeneratorError
12. non-ASCII stays UTF-8; ascii_only: true escapes it         "café" "caf\u00e9"
13. a Struct or a Time has no JSON shape: to_json is to_s, quoted "#<struct S x=1>" "2024-01-01 00:00:00 UTC"
14. YAML.dump({a: 1, "b" => [1, 2], c: nil}):                  
      ---
      :a: 1
      b:
      - 1
      - 2
      :c:
15. YAML.load: yes is true, ~ is nil, '1' stays a String       {"a" => 1, "b" => ["x"], "c" => true, "d" => nil, "e" => "1"}
16. YAML.load is safe: a !ruby/object tag raises               Psych::DisallowedClass: Tried to load unspecified class: Object
17.   YAML.unsafe_load builds it                               Object
18. Symbols are allowed; a Date is not until permitted_classes: :sym; Psych::DisallowedClass; Date
19. aliases are off by default; aliases: true allows them      Psych::AliasesNotEnabled; {"a" => 1, "b" => 1}
20. YAML round trip keeps Symbols and nesting                  {a: [1, {b: "c"}]}
21. Marshal.dump gives a binary String; dump(1) in hex; version String ASCII-8BIT; 04086906; 4.8
22. the round trip keeps Ruby types: Symbol, Range, Time       {a: [1, 2], c: 1..3, d: 2024-01-01 00:00:00 UTC}
23. load(dump(x)) is a deep copy: original, copy               {a: [1, [2]]}, {a: [1, [2, 3]]}
24. Marshal refuses a Proc and an IO                           TypeError: no _dump_data is defined for class Proc; can't dump IO
25. Marshal.load of garbage raises                             TypeError
26. TOML: no parser in Ruby's standard library                 LoadError: cannot load such file -- toml
